Hi, 
I was having a problem with using Rserve involving a command that takes a few moments to run and that also connects to the web to download some data. 
below is my code: 
it runs when I run it in R (as the commands not through Rserve) 
It runs when I run it locally on my windows laptop (local R and Rserve as well) 
but it dies when I run it on my remote installation of R and Rserve (from the server on my laptop) 
-it gives error 127 but this has not meaning to me 
the line that chokes it is: 
c.voidEval("opt <- yahoo.getOption(\"ELN\",\"2009-02\")"); 

if I comment out his line and change : 
c.voidEval("opt.mtx <- as.matrix(opt)"); 
to 
c.voidEval("opt.mtx <- as.matrix(mat)"); 
this work too! 

the line that chokes it causes (in R) the program to take about 5-10 seconds to download and process financial options information 
the line prior to it also does this but its just less data downloaded and is practically instant. 
Is there something I'm over looking? 
Any insight would be appreciated. And Id be happy to provide any clarifications. 
thanks 
-Casey 



Rconnection c = new Rconnection(host); 
REXP x = c.eval("R.version.string"); 
out.println("<br/>Rserve: <br/>" + x.asString() + "<br/>"); 

c.voidEval("source(\"http://www.fam.tuwien.ac.at/~mkeller/R-progs/yahoo_opt.R\")"); 
c.voidEval("mat <- yahoo.getMaturities(\"ELN\")"); 
c.voidEval("opt <- yahoo.getOption(\"ELN\",\"2009-02\")"); 
c.voidEval("opt.mtx <- as.matrix(opt)"); 
c.voidEval("opt1.mtx <- opt.mtx[1,1]"); 
String d = c.eval("opt1.mtx").asString(); 
out.println("<br/>Option Maturity: <br/>" +d); 

c.close();

